### app/views/brief_mailer/sunday_review.html.erb
<p><%= link_to "Re-authenticate with Schwab", @reauth_url %></p>
<p>Open it in Safari (not the home-screen app), sign in if asked, and tick every account on Schwab's consent screen: an account left unticked stops syncing.</p>
<% if @status.token %>
  <p>Token: <%= @status.token_status %>, issued <%= l(@status.token.issued_at, format: :connection) %>, expires <%= l(@status.token.refresh_expires_at, format: :connection) %></p>
<% else %>
  <p>Token: not connected</p>
<% end %>
<p><b>Feeds</b></p>
<ul>
  <% @status.feed_rows.each do |row| %><li><%= row.account.label %> · <%= row.feed %>: <%= row.latest ? "#{row.latest.status} #{l(row.latest.finished_at || row.latest.started_at, format: :weekday_time)}" : "never" %></li><% end %>
</ul>
<p>Failed sync runs, 7 days: <%= @status.failed_run_count %> · Failed jobs, 7 days: <%= @status.failed_job_count %></p>
<p><b>Setups</b></p>
<ul>
  <% @setups.each do |setup| %><li><%= setup.name %><%= " (inactive)" unless setup.active? %>: n=<%= setup.sample_size %>, win rate <%= setup.win_rate ? percent(setup.win_rate) : "n/a" %>, avg R <%= setup.avg_r ? number_with_precision(setup.avg_r, precision: 2) : "n/a" %>, expectancy <%= setup.expectancy ? number_with_precision(setup.expectancy, precision: 2) : "n/a" %></li><% end %>
  <% if @setups.empty? %><li>none defined yet</li><% end %>
</ul>
<p>The edge review itself (flagging negative-expectancy setups) arrives in Phase 2; the numbers above are the stored stats.</p>
<p><%= link_to "System", system_url %></p>

