 succeeded in 0ms:
docs/phase-1-plan.md:34:| 7 | `orders` | `account_id`, `instrument_id`, `broker_order_id` (unique per account), `status` enum incl. Phase 2 states, `side`, `quantity`, `filled_quantity`, `order_type`, `limit_price`, `stop_price`, `remaining_quantity`, `strategy_type` (SINGLE/TRIGGER/OCO, reconciliation needs it), `duration`, `session`, `tax_lot_method`, `placed_via` enum (schwab_direct/app), `parent_order_id` (self FK, bracket child), `replaces_order_id` (self FK, cancel/replace chain), `order_proposal_id` (nullable), `entered_at`, `closed_at`, `raw` jsonb. `instrument_id` is nullable for container strategies with no legs. Index on (account, instrument, entered_at) for Phase 2 reconciliation. An upsert never nulls a lineage or proposal column that already has a value | yes (sync only) |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:73:| `Sync::OrdersJob(account)` | via tick | Window: from = max(last `window_to` for this account − 1 day, now − 364 days), to = end of the current UTC day (bounds may be date-granular; verify item). First sync backfills a year (live probe confirmed the window). Flatten nested orders and upsert in two passes (rows, then lineage by broker id); container strategies are stored with no instrument; exactly 3000 rows means truncation and finishes `partial`. Any `positions.working_stop_order` not present in the response is re-fetched by id (covers old GTC stops, out-of-band cancels, and replacements outside the window). A daily `status: WORKING` pass. Then working-stop detection (§5) for every position, only on a complete run; a failed or partial run leaves stop assignments untouched |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:137:- Dividend or interest on an instrument with an open trade: `income` leg (feeds realized P&L, not basis). After close, attach to the most recent closed trade on that instrument within 90 days and recompute; otherwise journal with no leg. Return of capital is treated as income in Phase 1.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:141:- Sweeps, deposits, withdrawals, fees, and cash-only transfers: `journaled_at` set, no leg.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:215:- `Dockerfile`: no `EXPOSE` and no Thruster (dokku's nginx terminates TLS); Puma reads `PORT=5000`, and `bin/dokku-setup` pins `ports:set http:80:5000 https:443:5000` so the port map, the healthcheck, and the container agree. `BUNDLE_WITHOUT=development:test`. git stays in the runtime image for the `memory:pull` task in development.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:217:- Memory repo: the host owns the clone and the pull (PRD §5.6, "the VPS pulls the repo"); the container has no SSH client, no key, and `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0`, so an in-container pull of a private remote was never going to work. `Memory::CheckRepoJob` records every half hour what the mount holds (succeeded with the file count, failed when the mount is missing or empty, nothing when no path is configured); an empty mount is a degraded reason on the brief, never a crash. `Memory::Repo#pull!` remains for development (`bin/rails memory:pull`).
docs/phase-1-plan.md:220:- App time zone `Eastern Time (US & Canada)`; the container is UTC; recurring cron strings carry an explicit zone.
